 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
-*   **Precision**: The product of multiple PDFs can lead to underflow for long paths. Log-space arithmetic may be required.
-*   **Boundaries**: The geometry factor $G$ involves division by distance squared. If vertices are coincident ($\mathbf{y}_{i-1} = \mathbf{y}_i$), the value is undefined.
-*   **Degenerate Input**: Paths with $s < 2$ vertices do not have $i > 1$ cases.
